 <div class="card mb-3"><div class="card-header fw-semibold">4. Rate limits and errors</div><div class="card-body"><p>Each API client has a configurable request limit per minute. A 429 response includes <code>retry_after</code> and the <code>Retry-After</code> header. Common responses: 401 invalid token, 403 missing scope or revoked client, 422 invalid query/filter, 429 rate limit, 5xx service error.</p></div></div>
 <div class="card"><div class="card-header fw-semibold">5. Outbound Webhooks</div><div class="card-body"><p>Headers: <code>X-Webhook-Event</code> and <code>X-Webhook-Signature: sha256=...</code>. Signature is HMAC-SHA256 of the exact raw JSON request body using the one-time signing secret shown when the endpoint is created.</p><p class="mb-0">Delivery is asynchronous. Failed HTTP responses are retried with 30, 60 and 120 second backoff. Use a publicly reachable HTTPS endpoint; TLS verification is always enabled. Current event emitters: <code>customer.created</code>, <code>customer.updated</code>, <code>customer.suspended</code>, <code>customer.deleted</code> and <code>payment.received</code>.</p></div></div>
